1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:06,770
With HarvestSlot, a cassava farmer can agree on a buyer, a price and a pickup date before harvesting.

2
00:00:07,450 --> 00:00:09,573
Adunni signs up as a seller.

3
00:00:09,573 --> 00:00:13,820
Only the essentials are asked, and she lands on her own dashboard.

4
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:20,670
She adds her harvest: 2 tonnes of cassava in Akinyele, ready on 24 November.

5
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:26,973
HarvestSlot shows buyers with room on her dates.

6
00:00:26,973 --> 00:00:32,130
Moniya Garri Works can take all 2,000 kg, so she sends a request.

7
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:38,370
The buyer offers ₦100 per kg for the full quantity, and will collect from the farm.

8
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:46,110
Adunni sees every term in one place, then accepts.

9
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,500
The buyer’s space is now reserved, so it is safe to harvest.

10
00:00:55,400 --> 00:01:01,190
At collection, the buyer records the weight received and accepted: 1,900 kg.

11
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:06,890
Adunni is paid for what is accepted: ₦190,000.

12
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:11,120
The buyer pays by bank transfer, then records the transfer.

13
00:01:13,800 --> 00:01:17,921
It counts as paid only when Adunni confirms the money arrived.

14
00:01:17,921 --> 00:01:19,420
The sale is complete.

15
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:27,770
HarvestSlot. Agree on the sale before you harvest.

